gomodel:6ab067da00006950
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "OXM->GCGR: rat hepatocytes, OXM (1 uM) stimulates glycine cleavage flux, ~40% blocked by GCGR antagonist (PMID:9365819, abstract) -> ISS from rat Gcg/Gcgr. OXM is a low-affinity GCGR agonist; its main receptor is GLP1R. Supporting: hamster insulinoma OXM displaces glucagon binding (PMID:8828464); mouse OXM GCGR agonism/liver glycogenolysis (PMID:22421924)." , "PKA->CREB1 Ser133: PMID:2573431 (rat PC12) -> ISS RGD. CRTC2: mouse TORC2 regulates fasting gluconeogenic CREB transcription (PMID:16148943) -> ISS MGI. CREB1->PCK1/G6PC1: mouse CREB mutants reduce gluconeogenic gene expression (PMID:11557984) -> ISS MGI; note that in that study CREB acts largely via PGC-1 (not modelled). Not modelled: PKA-SIK2 control of CRTC2, CBP/p300, PGC-1alpha." , "Built by claude4go with curator 2026-10-12; source table reviewed and corrected (MF specificity, cAMP small-molecule link, one CREB1 unit per target, evidence). Mostly abstract-level evidence; full texts not read." , "2026-10-13: GCGR, GNAS, ADCY6, PKA moved from part_of GO:0007189 to part_of GO:0045722 'positive regulation of gluconeogenesis', same evidence as the glucagon model gomodel:6ab067da00007273 (see its comment: GCGR IDA PMID:35767325 + ISS MGI:99572; GNAS ISS MGI:95777 PMID:16239968; ADCY6 ISS MGI:87917 PMID:31918924, indirect; PKA ISS MGI:97592 PMID:23292513). OXM hormone activity deliberately LEFT on GO:0007189: PubMed search found no data showing native OXM drives gluconeogenesis (only rat hepatocyte glycine cleavage PMID:9365819, mouse glycogenolysis PMID:22421924, and synthetic OXM-based/dual-agonist pharmacology)." , "GNAS->ADCY6: human ADCY6 activated by Galpha-s in vitro (PMID:17110384, abstract; Gs species not stated) -> IC. ADCY6 choice for hepatocyte: mouse glucagon/ADCY6/cAMP/PKA/CREB pathway in hepatocytes (PMID:31918924)." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052" ;
        dc:date                "2026-11-10" ;
        dc:title               "Positive regulation of gluconeogenesis by OXM/GCGR (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" , "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00006950 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

